## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/h24/lt.png" alt="Lithuania" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', marginRight: '8px'}} />Lithuania

Lithuania maintains its foundational Western alignment while adapting to a more complex strategic environment. The country demonstrates continued Ukraine advocacy leadership with new institutional commitments (2027 EU presidency focus) while navigating Trump administration unpredictability through European coordination mechanisms. Defense cooperation continues expanding bilaterally within NATO framework. However, domestic democratic institutions face dual pressure from controversial coalition dynamics (Dawn of Nemunas partner misconduct) and unprecedented international scrutiny (European Parliament resolution on media freedom), creating new constraints on policy autonomy.

**Key developments:**

- **Diplomatic:** During official visit, Nausėda declared Ukraine's EU membership by 2030 a strategic Lithuanian interest and committed to focusing on Ukrainian accession during Lithuania's 2027 EU Council presidency. Discussed military cooperation and energy support with €1 billion in total military aid confirmed. *([ukrinform.net](https://ukrinform.net/rubric-polytics/4084210-nauseda-calls-ukraines-eu-membership-a-strategic-interest-for-lithuania.html), 2026-01-25)*
- **Diplomatic:** Nausėda publicly supported joint eight-nation European statement criticizing Trump's tariff threats over Greenland dispute with Denmark. Statement emphasized solidarity with Denmark and dialogue over confrontation. *([delfi.lt](https://delfi.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/nauseda-palaiko-europos-saliu-pareiskima-del-trumpo-grasinimu-120199865), 2026-01-20)*
- **Diplomatic:** Nausėda confirmed receiving informal invitation to join Trump's Board of Peace but stated Lithuania will consult Nordic-Baltic partners before deciding. Noted some participating countries' involvement 'seems grotesque' while keeping options open. *([lrt.lt](https://lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2814090/lithuania-to-consult-nb8-partners-on-joining-trump-s-board-of-peace-president), 2026-01-22)*
- **Domestic:** European Parliament passed resolution condemning Lithuania's LRT law amendments and expressing solidarity with public broadcaster. PM Ruginienė's advisor criticized Lithuanian MEPs for 'going the path of state discrediting,' while President Nausėda said EP resolutions cannot solve LRT's operational problems. *([etaplius.lt](https://etaplius.lt/aktualu/lietuva/i-ruginienes-patarejas-dalis-lietuvos-atstovu-ep-nusprende-eiti-valstybes-diskreditavimo-keliu/384291), 2026-01-24)*
- **Domestic:** Žemaitaitis physically pushed a young person during public meeting in Vilkaviškyje library. PM Ruginienė's office condemned the behavior, generating political commentary about governance standards with coalition partner. *([lrt.lt](https://lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2812867/zemaiciaitis-susistumdavo-su-jaunuoliu-vilkaviskyje-ruginienes-kanceliarija-smeike-tokg-elgesi), 2026-01-22)*

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Zelensky makes official visit to Lithuania, discusses EU membership and energy support** — Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky visited Lithuania for official talks with President Nausėda. They discussed Ukraine's EU accession prospects, with Nausėda supporting membership by 2030, energy system support, and military cooperation. First ladies also met for humanitarian cooperation talks. *([lrt.lt](https://lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2817007/nauseda-susitikime-su-zelenskiu-lietuva-visada-isliks-tarp-aktyviausiu-ukrainos-remeju))*
- **Lithuania supports European statement criticizing Trump's Greenland tariff threats** — President Nausėda expressed support for a joint European statement criticizing US President Trump's threats to impose tariffs on countries supporting Denmark in the Greenland dispute. Nausėda suggested joint security arrangements could resolve the standoff and emphasized cooperation over confrontation. *([reuters.com](https://reuters.com/world/europe/lithuania-president-says-joint-security-deal-could-end-greenland-row-2026-01-20))*
- **Dawn of Nemunas leader Žemaitaitis involved in physical altercation in Vilkaviškyje** — Remigijus Žemaitaitis, leader of the governing coalition partner Dawn of Nemunas, physically pushed a young person during a public meeting in Vilkaviškyje library. PM Ruginienė's office condemned the behavior, leading to political commentary about governance standards. *([lrt.lt](https://lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2811365/zemaitaitis-apsistumde-vilkaviskyje-iskviesta-policija-sureagavo-ir-premjeres-komanda))*
- **Eurovision national selection reveals first finalists with Rug!lė leading competition** — Lithuania's Eurovision national selection progressed with the first two finalists announced. Rug!lė emerged as the early leader, while other contestants like Nøra Blu presented their entries for the competition to select Lithuania's Eurovision representative. *([lrt.lt](https://lrt.lt/naujienos/muzika/680/2815175/paaiskejo-du-pirmieji-eurovizija-lt-finalininkai-lydere-tapo-rug-le))*
- **Conservative party shifts tone under new leader Kasčiūnas, moving away from perceived arrogance** — The opposition Homeland Union (TS-LKD) has changed its approach under new chairman Laurynas Kasčiūnas, adopting a more collaborative and less confrontational style compared to previous leadership, with analysts noting reduced arrogance and increased willingness to engage across party lines. *([15min.lt](https://15min.lt/naujiena/aktualu/lietuva/maziau-arogancijos-daugiau-flirto-kasciunas-gali-ir-patyleti-ir-gali-kalbeti-su-visais-56-2604500))*
</Accordion>


